# provision/vps/sudoers/rumaq-scraper-deploy — the deploy identity's entire
# root grant for the RumaQ scraper, installed by provision/vps/apply.sh at
# /etc/sudoers.d/rumaq-scraper-deploy (root:root 0440, only after the
# candidate passes `visudo -cf`).
#
# The deploy identity is the box-wide shared `kajianq-deploy` account
# (homepage MACHINE.md); its powers are scoped per app by fragments like
# this one. The RumaQ VPS deploy needs exactly ONE privileged operation:
# start the post-deploy self-check unit, which runs as the service user and
# reads the root-only env file through systemd — the deploy itself never
# reads /etc/rumaq-scraper/env. (Plus the agent restart below.)
#
# Operations (owner decision 2026-10-27) — restarting/re-arming the nightly
# job and repairing the env's ingest URL must work without an interactive
# sudo (the operator's password stays out of every loop):
#   - start rumaq-scraper.service         trigger a run now (both blocking
#     and --no-block forms, matched exactly)
#   - reset-failed rumaq-scraper.service  clear a stale failed state
#   - restart rumaq-scraper-agent.service the Scrape Now agent runs the code
#     the deploy just shipped; a restart loads it immediately (the agent is
#     an idle poller until a command is queued, so the restart is safe)
#   - /usr/local/sbin/rumaq-scraper-ingest-url
#     root-owned helper (installed by apply.sh, no arguments) that points
#     the env's RUMAQ_INGEST_URL at the production ingest route. The URL is
#     public repo knowledge; the env's key lines are never touched. No new
#     risk: kajianq-deploy already owns the code tree it ships.
#
# Code deploys need no grant beyond the agent restart: the deploy identity
# owns /srv/rumaq-scraper (code + browser cache); the nightly job is a
# timer-driven oneshot that picks up new code at its next start, and the
# agent (the only long-lived process) is restarted right above. Exact
# command, absolute path, no wildcards: wildcard arguments in sudoers are
# the classic privilege-escalation footgun.

Defaults:kajianq-deploy !requiretty

kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start rumaq-scraper-selfcheck.service
kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start rumaq-scraper.service
kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl start --no-block rumaq-scraper.service
kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl reset-failed rumaq-scraper.service
kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart rumaq-scraper-agent.service
kajianq-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/local/sbin/rumaq-scraper-ingest-url
